WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.600
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. So 2016 seems destined to be remembered as the year of the Dumpster fire.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.860
But I don't really think that's fair, because like anything, 2016 is

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.060
vast and it contains multitudes. Like really 2016 wasn' t even one year, it was

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.940
7.4 billion different years to 7.4 billion different people.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.340
Anyway, Rosianna recently asked her viewers to share their "Best of 2016" and I found it so encouraging

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.800
to hear about all the wonderful expiriences people had this year, so I thought today I would share

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.180
my four favourite memories of 2016.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.480
First: I got to attend the 100th running of the Indy 500 with my mom and dad and lots of our friends.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.900
Now I know, that the Indy 500 is technically just 800 left turns, half of which you can't see

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.160
because the track is so huge.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.300
But it is also the largest non-religious gathering of human beings on Earth.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.940
And while I'm not usually a crowds person, it is truly wondrous to see so many different people come together.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.020
And then I left the Indy 500, drove to the airport and boarded a plane to go to London,

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:01.860
where I got to see Nerdfighteria-sponsored AFC Wimbledon play at Wembley for a spot in the third tier of English football.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:08.280
A game which they won, and then sleepless and delirious I returned to Wimbledon's home stadium to party

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.280
with my dad and friends and strangers and AFC Wimbledon players

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.720
and it was just magical.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:19.120
Now again one could easily say: How could you get so exited about the 82nd best football team in England?

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:23.900
And to those people I would say: "At the moment AFC Wimbledon are actually the 55th best football team in England".

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.160
Second great memory of 2016: Sarah's cousin getting married in Portland, Oregon.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:34.280
So when Sarah and I were in our twenties we sometimes went to seven or eight weddings a year and frankly, I came to dread them.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:41.420
Because you know, I dislike formal wear and banquet food and making small-talk with strangers and overly long toasts and most of all dancing.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:47.220
But now that we've reached an age where weddings are few and far between, I've really come around to them and this one in particular had me

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.840
both laughing and crying.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.380
I'd known the groom since he was in high school; the couple were lovely and generous to each other

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.440
and to their guests.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.860
It was so fun to watch my kids watch a wedding, because they were just like:

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.900
"Dad? What is happening?"

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.720
And best of all after the wedding we got to go to a Portland Timbers game.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.240
Third great memory of 2016:

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.140
Meeting Baby Orin in Montana.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.480
Hank,  I don't want to taunt you by bragging about experiences that you can't have

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.040
But there is nothing like the pride and happiness of seeing your baby brother be

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.180
such a commited and loving father.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.980
Hank, in your life you've been good at many things, but when I was visiting with you and Katherine and Orin in Montana

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.040
I thought: he's found the thing that he's best at.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:28.220
Okay, enough sentimentality. So far, all my favorite memories of 2016 involved leaving Indianapolis and that's not a good sign.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.840
And while I do dearly love our airport, named best airport in America four years running

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.880
I think my favorite memory of this year was being home. In both 2014 and 2015

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.900
I spend more than a hundred days away from home. This year I was home nine nights out of ten.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.220
That meant more time for writing, and more time  with my family and while I think

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.400
quality time with your kids is incredibly important

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.040
there's also something to be said for quantity time.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.800
And this was an awesome year to be a dad.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.980
Henry learned how to ride a bike,

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.520
Alice learned her ABCs,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.940
they both learned every single word to Moana,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.100
and I was home for most of it, which was the best thing to happen to me this year, other than AFC Wimbledon's promotion.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:07.500
Nerdfighters, if you'd like to share your best of 2016, please do so in comments, or make a video and link to it in comments.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:14.700
Hank, when you see me next, it will be 2017, meaning that the vlogbrothers channel will be celebrating its tenth anniversary.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.200
Thank you for doing this with me for a decade!

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.660
What a long strange trip it has been, I will see you on Tuesday.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.340
Friday, dang it! SO bad at days!

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.860
When you gonna learn that, Green? When are you gonna get your days down?

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.060
*heavy sigh*

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:38.260
I've reached that age, where my son has suddenly surpassed me in ability to tell what day of the week it is it is.

